{"t": 1795071942.4171689, "kind": "assistant", "text": "The PHP upgrade to 8.3 caused a fatal error in the `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` plugin. I must stop here and report this plugin incompatibility.\n\n**Production change plan:**\n\nWe **cannot** upgrade to PHP 8.3 on production until the `limit-login-attempts-reloaded` plugin is fixed or replaced, because it causes a fatal error.\n\n**Next steps for the human:**\n1. Check the plugin's compatibility with PHP 8.3 (check updates, compatibility tickets, or the plugin's support forum).\n2. If an updated version exists, update the plugin on **dev** first, retest PHP 8.3, and confirm the site works.\n3. If no compatible version exists, consider a replacement plugin (e.g., **Limit Login Attempts 2** or **Login Lockout**) — install and configure it on **dev**, then test PHP 8.3 again.\n4. After successful testing on dev with PHP 8.3 and the working login-limit solution, I can propose the final production change.\n\nUntil the plugin issue is resolved, PHP 8.3 cannot be applied to production."}
